{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462350-minor-milestones-shifting-skills","id":462350,"title":"Minor Milestones - Shifting Skills","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-30T09:25:14-07:00","id":462350,"title":"Minor Milestones - Shifting Skills","content":"On top of the Werewolf game my group is running, we're also playing a Fate Core system based game. There's a feature in Fate that I've not seen explicitly written in other games, but seems like a good idea.<br /> <br /> Specifically, at the end of each session of Fate, you hit a Minor Milestone and get to swap two of your skills around to reflect things you're using more now without actually getting more powerful overall.<br /> The only real mapping of that I see in World of Darkness is the Sanctity of Merits, wherein if something happens to make your Merits not make sense, you can change what they were for.<br /> Given that dots allocated to the second-through-fifth positions no longer cost more than their first-dot counterparts, being able to shift dots around now and again wouldn't be a mechanical nightmare. Say your character has been ignoring his studies to get ready for the big fight, maybe he could drop a dot of Academics and pick up one in Brawl. Regarless of whether the dot was a fifth dot or a first dot, you're dropping a 2XP thing for another 2XP thing.<br /> <br /> Has anyone run with anything like this? If so, how'd you handle it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T09:54:22-07:00","id":462380,"title":"","content":"Is there a limit for this? Could I swap my 3 dots in Politics for my 1 in Brawl?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T10:21:51-07:00","id":462398,"title":"","content":"In the other system, its a swap two things once per session sort of thing, typically with the assumption that you'd be switching a 0 with a 1 or a 3 with a 4.<br /> So by a direct application, no, I guess. On the first night you'd change both to 2s and then on the second night you'd be ready for the fight as it were.<br /> <br /> It makes some nerative sense if your character is very focused on one particular skill, but it seems like the kind of thing that wouldn't happen overnight.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T12:22:05-07:00","id":462579,"title":"","content":"Is it something you could do over a couple sessions? Our sessions sometimes take place in the same night, so how would that work out?<br /> <br /> And it turns out my Politics is at 2 dots, so could I switch that with my Brawl which is at 1 dot the first session, then switch my new 2 dots of Brawl with my 3 dots of Crafts at the second session?<br /> <br /> It seems like I'd have a huge advantage if at character creation I skills at 1, 2, 3, 4 and 5 dots. Providing I didn't get my primal urge very high, I could just rotate around to get 5 skill points in whatever I thought was necessary in a few sessions and never have to learn a new skill again.<br /> <br /> In this system, are you unable to advance your skill points once the game has begun or something?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-30-2015, 03:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T12:51:16-07:00","id":462616,"title":"","content":"To start with your last question first, in that system you advance a skill at more significant milestones. In WoD terms, the shifting stuff around happens at the end of each Chapter (session) and a skill-up advancement happens at the end of each Story (handful of related sessions). Every handful of stories there's a bigger advancement action, too. That's pretty much the whole of the XP mechanic for the system, though.<br /> <br /> My thoughts on applying the minor milestone idea to WoD wouldn't require two stats being next to each other when you switch them (you do have skills at all the different ratings in the other one, though), just so long as you're only moving one dot around at a time. So if you've got a 5 in Firearms, but you spend more time in a story chatting people up than you do shooting, maybe you could drop the 5th dot in Firearms for a first dot in Socialize. So they'd be at 4 and 1 when they had been at 5 and 0.<br /> I don't really know how it would play out, whether it would make for overpowered people or just make the game confusing, or if it would make things make more sense.<br /> <br /> Has anyone tried it before?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T12:55:11-07:00","id":462618,"title":"","content":"You earn Additional Skill points with a Significant or Major Milestone...<br /> You must keep your skills tiered, as well (whether as a pyramid or a ladder).<br /> <br /> It is a very elegant system, and I tend to prefer it over nWOD for many things (though nWOD has its place, to be sure). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-30T13:50:25-07:00","id":462647,"title":"","content":"Have you tried applying the Minor Milestones principal to nWoD, though, was more my question.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T12:31:31-07:00","id":463726,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462350-minor-milestones-shifting-skills?p=462398#post462398\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the other system, its a swap two things once per session sort of thing, typically with the assumption that you'd be switching a 0 with a 1 or a 3 with a 4.<br /> So by a direct application, no, I guess. On the first night you'd change both to 2s and then on the second night you'd be ready for the fight as it were.<br /> <br /> It makes some nerative sense if your character is very focused on one particular skill, but it seems like the kind of thing that wouldn't happen overnight.</div> </div> </div> </div>In my Dresden Files game, the guy with Resources +4 would regularly drop it a point to raise one of his +3 skills, stating that he was tying money up in boosting the skill through bribes, special equipment, etc. I thought it was a good use of the Minor Milestone swap.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-31T15:31:18-07:00","id":463946,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/462350-minor-milestones-shifting-skills?p=462647#post462647\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Have you tried applying the Minor Milestones principal to nWoD, though, was more my question.</div> </div> </div> </div>No - If I was wanting such things (and I generally do, most of the time), I would rather prefer to play Fate than importing the mechanic into an nWOD game. I have a current port into the Fate System for my nWOD campaign city. Honestly, the system works far better than the 2nd Edition GMC rule set seems too. But that is just me.<br /> <br /> Of course, I am always willing to get back to our San Francisco Game (which is 1st Edition nWOD). <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}